 ## Serve
 - `bin/serve`: `db:prepare` + `assets:precompile` + `rails server -b 0.0.0.0 -p $PORT -e production` (foreground). Handles `PORT`, `SECRET_KEY_BASE`, `QUIZZY_*` from env.
+
+## Export / Import (2026-10-08)
+- Routes: `GET /moderate/import` (`moderate_import_path`, `Imports#new`), `POST /moderate/import` (`Imports#create`), `GET /moderate/quizzes/:id/export` (`export_moderate_quiz_path`, `Quizzes#export`). Both require moderator basic auth via `Moderate::BaseController`.
+- Quiz page (`quizzes/show`): added `Export` link next to `Preview` (`<a>Export</a>` → export page).
+- Index (`quizzes/index`): added `Import quiz` button next to `New quiz` (`<a>Import quiz</a>` → import page).
+- Export page (`quizzes/export.html.erb`): single `<pre>` (only one on page) with `JSON.pretty_generate({"title"=>, "questions"=>[{"text"=>, "active"=>, "options"=>[{"text"=>, "correct"=>}]}]})`. Keys in that order, exactly those keys, booleans always written, order by `position,id`. Uses `<%= @export_json %>` (HTML-escaped, `textContent` decodes to valid JSON).
+- Import page (`imports/new.html.erb`): `<label for="quiz_json">Quiz JSON</label>` + `<textarea id="quiz_json" name="quiz_json">` + `<button>Import</button>` POST to `/moderate/import`. No `required` so invalid/empty JSON reaches server validation. Errors shown in `.errors > ul > li`, status 422, textarea retains input.
+- Import logic (`Moderate::ImportsController#validate_import`): `JSON.parse`, require Hash, `title` String non-blank else `Title can't be blank`, `questions` Array else `Questions must be an array`. Per question `Qn`: must be Hash, `text` String non-blank else `Question N: Question can't be blank`, `active` optional default `true` (if present must be boolean else `Question N: Active must be true or false`), `options` Array else `Question N: Options must be an array`. Per option: must be Hash, `text` missing/nil→`""` else must be String (strip), `correct` optional default `false` (if present must be boolean). Then same rules as question form on non-empty (strip present) options: `<2` → `Question N: Add at least two options`, none correct → `Question N: Mark at least one option as correct`. Unknown keys ignored. All errors collected; on any error render `new` 422 with no DB writes.
+- Creation is atomic: `ActiveRecord::Base.transaction` + `create!` with explicit `position` (1..N preserving JSON order). Always `Quiz.create!` (never find-or-update, duplicate titles create new rows). Trim title/text/option text. Redirect to `moderate_quiz_path(new_quiz)` on success (opens its page).
+- Round-trip verified: export → import → export yields identical parsed JSON; defaults (`active:true`, `correct:false`) verified via DB and re-export.
